---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — BenihKode" description="BenihKode is a solo developer studio that builds small, opinionated developer tools — CLIs, npm packages, browser extensions, and apps — and documents the engineering behind them.">
	<section style="padding-top: 4rem;">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-label">About</div>
			<h1 class="section-title animate-on-scroll">The Story Behind BenihKode</h1>
			<div class="about-content animate-on-scroll">
				<p class="about-summary">
					<strong>BenihKode is a solo developer studio that builds small, opinionated developer tools</strong> —
					CLIs, npm packages, browser extensions, and mobile apps — then documents the engineering
					behind each one. The name means "Seed of Code": every shipped tool starts as a small idea
					and grows in public.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>BenihKode</strong> means "Seed of Code" — a name that reflects the philosophy that every great application begins as a tiny idea, a seed that needs nurturing, patience, and care to grow into something real and meaningful.
				</p>
				<p>
					This is a developer's garden — a place where ideas are planted as Product Requirement Documents, nurtured through development, and eventually harvested as shipped products. Along the way, the journey is documented through honest journal entries about the joys, frustrations, and breakthroughs of building software.
				</p>
				<h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Product Ideas 💡</strong> — Seeds waiting to be planted. Full PRDs with visions, specs, and dreams.</li>
					<li><strong>Shipped Projects 🚀</strong> — From seed to harvest. Real projects that made it out of the garden.</li>
					<li><strong>Dev Journal 📝</strong> — Notes, learnings, and stories from the trenches. Growing in public.</li>
				</ul>
				<h2>What BenihKode Ships</h2>
				<p>
					The current toolset spans command-line utilities and apps. Every tool is free and
					open-source, published on npm or the relevant store, and documented on its own page.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>gitcommitgen</strong> — AI-powered conventional commit messages from staged changes.</li>
					<li><strong>gitprgen</strong> — AI-generated pull request descriptions from git diffs.</li>
					<li><strong>gitprune</strong> — safe git branch cleanup without losing work.</li>
					<li><strong>secretsweep</strong> — zero-config secret scanning for staged files.</li>
					<li><strong>jsonask</strong> — query JSON in natural language instead of jq.</li>
					<li><strong>mcpkit</strong> — generate MCP servers from OpenAPI specs, databases, or YAML.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The full list, with install commands and source repositories, is on the
					<a href="/tools/">Developer Tools</a> page.
				</p>

				<h2>Find BenihKode Elsewhere</h2>
				<ul class="about-profiles">
					<li><a href="https://github.com/BenihDev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> — source for every tool</li>
					<li><a href="https://twitter.com/benihkode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X / Twitter</a></li>
					<li><a href="https://linkedin.com/company/benihkode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a></li>
				</ul>

				<h2>The Philosophy</h2>
				<p>
					Not every seed becomes a tree. Some ideas stay as seeds, some start growing but pivot into something else entirely, and some bloom beautifully. The point isn't perfection — it's the act of planting, nurturing, and learning from every attempt.
				</p>
				<p>
					This garden is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, powered by <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com">Cloudflare</a>, and designed with a love for clean code and thoughtful interfaces.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-content {
		max-width: 680px;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}
	.about-content p {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
	}
	.about-summary {
		font-size: 1.08rem;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	.about-profiles li a {
		color: var(--accent);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
	.about-content h2 {
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.about-content ul {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	.about-content li {
		padding: 0.75rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}
	.about-content li strong {
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}
	.about-content a {
		color: var(--accent);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
